    "text": "To find the value of \\((x + 1 - x)! \\div (x - x + 1)!\\) in simplest form, we will proceed step by step.\n\nFirst, simplify the expressions inside the factorials:\n\\[\nx + 1 - x = 1\n\\]\n\\[\nx - x + 1 = 1\n\\]\n\nThus, the expression becomes:\n\\[\n1! \\div 1!\n\\]\n\nNext, recall that the factorial of 1 is 1:\n\\[\n1! = 1\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the expression simplifies to:\n\\[\n1! \\div 1! = \\frac{1}{1} = 1\n\\]\n\nSo, the value of \\((x + 1 - x)! \\div (x - x + 1)!\\) in simplest form is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}\n\\]",
